/-- **ν and an optimal pose of `Johnson.AugmentedTruncatedCube.polyhedron` as one root**: when the representatives' systems have
exactly one root each, of scale `N`, the system `S` has exactly one root, of scale `N`, and at it
`matAt x 67`, `matAt x 58` and `(x 76, x 77)` are a weak fit of `Johnson.AugmentedTruncatedCube.polyhedron` scaled
by `N` through itself. -/
theorem johnsonAugmentedTruncatedCube_pose_of_reps {N : ℝ} (h : PolynomialSystem.IsRootEq [Pose.JohnsonAugmentedTruncatedCube.reps0] N) :
    PolynomialSystem.IsPoseRoot Johnson.AugmentedTruncatedCube.polyhedron Pose.JohnsonAugmentedTruncatedCube.S N 67 58 76 := by
  rw [Pose.JohnsonAugmentedTruncatedCube.S_eq]
  exact PolynomialSystem.ct_isPoseRoot h List.mem_cons_self Pose.JohnsonAugmentedTruncatedCube.len_eq Pose.JohnsonAugmentedTruncatedCube.reps_eq
    (Root.ParData.sqrt_spec (by decide +kernel)) Pose.JohnsonAugmentedTruncatedCube.par_ok Pose.JohnsonAugmentedTruncatedCube.zs_eq Pose.JohnsonAugmentedTruncatedCube.weak_ok Pose.JohnsonAugmentedTruncatedCube.poly_eq Pose.JohnsonAugmentedTruncatedCube.ok

end Nieuwland.Polyhedra
